      "writtenOn": "2023-01-16T10:38:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not a great helper function. It is safe in the context of today\u0027s users but not in general. It only does what the name says if the input is a null-terminated string, but there is no such requirement or check. It will also panic if you give it an empty slice.\n\nOption 1) Turn it into `PartitionName::as_bytes`, similar to your `as_cstr`, and compare the partition name slice against `PartitionName::InitrdABC.as_bytes()`.\n\nOption 2) Implement this as `PartitionName::from_bytes`. That way you can first convert the partition name slice to an enum value and then have a `PartitionName::is_initrd` to do the final check.\n\nI would actually prefer option 2. `partition_name_matches_initrd` feels like it\u0027s mixing type conversion with policy.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 377,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 377,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "46cb712ec944568aae9af1e519f1c943b40d9a78",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
